/// First [`BC6H_BIT_LAYOUTS`] index of each mode. The values follow from the
/// `comp == -1` sentinels that terminate each mode's program in the flattened
/// table; a unit test rederives them by scanning, so a regenerated table with
/// different mode lengths fails the test instead of silently misindexing.
/// (Spelled out rather than const-evaluated: on the crate's MSRV a const fn
/// cannot read a static.)
pub static BC6H_LAYOUT_OFFSETS: [usize; 14] = [
    0, 21, 46, 66, 88, 110, 131, 152, 175, 198, 223, 230, 240, 250,
];

/// The 32 BC6H two-subset partition patterns, flattened to one row per pattern
/// scanline: texel `i` of pattern `p` is
/// `[p * 4 + i / 4][i % 4]`. The low bit is the subset index; bit 7 flags an
/// anchor texel, whose weight is stored with one less bit.
